  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" para="true">IOH. FRIDERICI FAVSTI</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="1">AB ASCHAFFENBVRGO,</l>
    <l n="3" type="heading" level="1">PATRICII ET SENATORIS</l>
    <l n="4" type="heading" level="1">FRANCOFORDIANI,</l>
    <l n="5" type="heading" level="1">ODE AD MELCHIOREM HAIMINSFELDIVM</l>
    <l n="6" type="heading" level="1">GOLDASTVM.</l>
    <l n="7" para="true">[?]Inon minori laude vehendus</l>
    <l n="8">est, Inuenta quisquis sedulus excolit,</l>
    <l n="9">Formaque donat, atque lucis</l>
    <l n="10">Perspicuæ probitate vestit.</l>
    <l n="11">Næ clariori laude vehendus</l>
    <l n="12">est, Qui scripta, longi conscia temporis,</l>
    <l n="13">At pressa tristibus tenebris,</l>
    <l n="14">Eruit atque situ repurgat.</l>
    <l n="15">Vtinde seris magna nepotibus</l>
    <l n="16">Virtus parentum, factaque fortia,</l>
    <l n="17">Cultusque constent literarum,</l>
    <l n="18">Obsequiis imitanda pulchris.</l>
    <l n="19">Id tu reponis dotibus ingeni</l>
    <l n="20">HAIMSFELDIANI gloria sanguinis,</l>
    <l n="21">Reddisque luci, quæ tenebris</l>
    <l n="22">Obruta delituere multis.</l>
    <l n="23">Sic, macte famâ, vindicias age</l>
    <l n="24">Feré sepultæ laudis, &amp; optumum</l>
    <l n="25">Serua decus peritioris</l>
    <l n="26">Teutoniæ, calamo perenni.</l>
    <l n="27">O si diebus præteritis, patrum</l>
    <l n="28">Fuisset hæc industria, curaque,</l>
    <l n="29">Non erudita tot virorum</l>
    <l n="30">Scripta nigris tegerentur vmbris:</l>
    <l n="31">Nec facta ficta, fortis &amp; inclutæ</l>
    <l n="32">Germaniæ, caligine perderet,</l>
    <l n="33">Sed campo inglorius Notator</l>
    <l n="34">Iulius eiiceretur omni.</l>
    <l n="35" para="true">SYLLA-</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The first letter S is a large woodcut initial, transcribed as "I" plus "non" is the printed first word "Inon" resolved as "Non" with the initial; the initial letter is uncertain. Lines are printed as verse; each stanza-like block is one paragraph. Words in the verse with doubtful letters are marked [?].</notes>
